# Scacelith - Latviešu
#
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals have three forms, in this order:
# zero (0, 10-20, 30...: n%10 = 0 or n%100 = 11-19)|one (1, 21, 31...: n%10 = 1 but not 11)|other.
# A "zero" number does not decline: alone (nominative) its noun is in the genitive plural
# ("10 partiju", as the coach files count); after a preposition the noun takes that preposition's
# case ("pēc 10 gājieniem", "pēc 1 gājiena", "pēc 3 gājieniem").
# Register: formal "jūs" (lowercase mid-sentence), as Latvian Microsoft/Apple software; buttons and
# menu entries in the infinitive ("Saglabāt", "Padoties"); sentence case, titles in capitals.
# The player's gender is unknown: finite verbs ("Jūs uzvarējāt", "Jūs izrakstījāties"), never a
# participle or adjective agreeing with the player. A name placeholder never takes a case ending:
# it stands in the nominative ("{0}: karodziņš nokrita", "Vai {0} padodas?").
# Chess terms: glossary of the translation (Latvijas Šaha federācija): karalis, dāma, tornis, laidnis,
# zirgs, bandinieks (K D T L Z); šahs, mats, pats, neizšķirts, rokāde, partija, pieraksta lapa.
# Keep the sections: other parts of the game add their keys in sections of their own.

